D75FFF]◆ EPIC sase-16n[/bold #D75FFF]\n[dim]  Title: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]Xprompt project tags (+sase)[/bold #D7AFFF]\n[dim]   Goal: [#D7D7AF][/dim]Prompts name their project with a `+<project>` project tag by [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]default. SASE resolves the tag to the project's VCS type and runs [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]the same `#gh:`/`#git:` workflow as before. Every completion [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]surface (TUI, LSP/Neovim, shell) inserts tags. Every surface that [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]shows raw prompts renders tags in the project's accent color. [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]Project names are enforced unique, case-insensitively, across all [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]VCS types.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]10[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]6[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202609/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]project_tags.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202609/project_tags.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-16n[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-16n/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]sase-core project tag lexer, resolver, expander, and bindings[/bold #D7AFFF] [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]core-tags[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]core-tags: add the sase_core project_tag module (tag scanning with [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]literal-zone skipping, anchored-position detection, case-insensitive [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]resolution with suggestions, in-place expansion to VCS refs, completion [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]trigger and selection-apply), the v5 catalog wire types, and Python [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]bindings.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Case-insensitive project name uniqueness across VCS types[/bold #D7AFFF]     [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]unique-names[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]unique-names: make every write-time project ref check case-insensitive [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and reserve home. Widen doctor project.name_collisions to every [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]key/name/alias conflict, and mirror the rule in sase-core collision [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]warnings and sase-github name allocation. Then verify this machine has [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]no collisions.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Python project tag backend and launch integration[/bold #D7AFFF]             [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]backend[dim] · [dim][/dim]after core-tags, unique-names[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]backend: shared accent module, cached project tag catalog, expansion [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]inside prompt canonicalization and launch_query, launch-unit validation,[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]tag-aware helpers for raw-text consumers, generators that default to [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]tags, and the v5 LSP catalog payload. Also moves the core pin.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]sase-xprompt-lsp project tag support[/bold #D7AFFF]                          [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]lsp[dim] · [dim][/dim]after core-tags[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]lsp: tag completion with in-place edits, semantic tokens with accent [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]modifiers plus a palette capability, hover, diagnostics, quick fixes and[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]a rewrite-to-tag code action, and leading-project detection that [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]understands tags.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]TUI prompt editor completion and tag defaults[/bold #D7AFFF]                 [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]tui-editor[dim] · [dim][/dim]after backend[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]tui-editor: the + trigger through the core binding, in-place accept, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]accent-styled completion rows ordered current-project-first, tag [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]prefills and MRU cycling, editor project context from tags, pre-submit [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]tag validation, and shell completion for +.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Tag rendering in the agent panel and prompt editor[/bold #D7AFFF]            [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]tag-display[dim] · [dim][/dim]after tui-editor[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]tag-display: the humanizer renders project refs as tags; the shared [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]tokenizer emits project_tag spans; accent styles in both highlight [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]systems; the prompt editor, the AGENT XPROMPT sections (main, family, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]hint, and clan), and their visual snapshots.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  7 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Accent-colored tags on every remaining raw-prompt surface[/bold #D7AFFF]     [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]tag-surfaces[dim] · [dim][/dim]after tag-display[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]tag-surfaces: prompt history, stash, launch approval, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]runners/revive/run-log previews, the metadata pager, the ACE query [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]+project shorthand, CLI prompt output, and the sase project list/show [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]TAG column and JSON fields.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  8 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]sase-nvim project tag highlighting and picker[/bold #D7AFFF]                 [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]nvim[dim] · [dim][/dim]after lsp, backend[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]nvim: accent highlight groups built from the server palette, a [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]semantic-token handler for saseProjectTag, + support in the Ctrl+T [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]picker, README, and smoke tests.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  9 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]sase-telegram and sase-github tag adoption[/bold #D7AFFF]                    [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]plugins[dim] · [dim][/dim]after tag-display[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]plugins: Telegram project-context capture and copy-text buttons use [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]tags, its inbound docs and tests are updated, and sase-github docs [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]present +<project> as the default.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  10 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Docs, skills, memory, config, and machine verification[/bold #D7AFFF]       [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]docs-memory[dim] · [dim][/dim]after unique-names, tui-editor, tag-surfaces, nvim, [/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#AF87FF][dim]plugins[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]docs-memory: docs and CLI help move to +<project>; fix the sase_run [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]skill example; add the Project Tag glossary strand and update the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]sase-project and xprompts notes; drop redundant chezmoi gh_* xprompt [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]shortcuts; run the final doctor verification on this machine.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-16n","llm_provider":"muse","model":"muse-spark-1.3-contributor","patch_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","phase_bead_id":"sase-16n.1","reasoning_effort":"xhigh","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},"source_run_id":"run-27a28298ce107d0720b0ce572e26a8d5","started_at":"2026-09-22T22:51:56.988945+00:00","state":